\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The ill-typed catalogue the checker rejects. Errors\nobreakspace  {}6 and\nobreakspace  {}10 are the provenance and guarantee-grade violations; the stage-ordering errors of Corollary\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {cor:order} (gadgetize-before-choice, emit-before-layout, decode-from- $\setbox \z@ \hbox {\mathsurround \z@ $\textstyle \mathsf  {UDG}$}\mathaccent "0365{\mathsf  {UDG}}$) are rejected structurally by the absence of an applicable rule. The language test suite exercises a representative subset and confirms each is raised.}}{16}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:errors}{{3}{16}{The ill-typed catalogue the checker rejects. Errors~6 and~10 are the provenance and guarantee-grade violations; the stage-ordering errors of Corollary~\ref {cor:order} (gadgetize-before-choice, emit-before-layout, decode-from- $\tUDGa $) are rejected structurally by the absence of an applicable rule. The language test suite exercises a representative subset and confirms each is raised}{table.3}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Reduction validated by simulation. Each graph is run at $k=\chi $ and $k=\chi {-}1$; all $18$ simulated instances reproduce the brute-force oracle's $\alpha (G')$ exactly, and every $k=\chi $ case decodes to a proper coloring. The $k=\chi {-}1$ rows (omitted for space) likewise match, correctly reporting non-colorability. Petersen exceeds the $16$-slot classical-simulation wall.}}{16}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:sim}{{4}{16}{Reduction validated by simulation. Each graph is run at $k=\chi $ and $k=\chi {-}1$; all $18$ simulated instances reproduce the brute-force oracle's $\indep (G')$ exactly, and every $k=\chi $ case decodes to a proper coloring. The $k=\chi {-}1$ rows (omitted for space) likewise match, correctly reporting non-colorability. Petersen exceeds the $16$-slot classical-simulation wall}{table.4}{}}
